Kylie Jenner and Forbes might be feuding  over her billionaire status but the  magazine still gave her the number-one  spot on their 2020 celeb 100 list which  ranks the world's highest-paid celebs  based on annual pay thank you the list  was released on Thursday and according  to Forbes the 22 year old earned five  hundred and ninety million dollars over  the past year which can mostly be  attributed to Cody buying a 51% stake of  Kylie cosmetics last January she sold it  for a whopping 600 million dollars which  led to her earning five hundred and  forty million dollars pre-tax she works  really hard the mag also named Kylie's  brother-in-law Kanye West as the second  highest-paid celeb this year according  to Forbes he earned one hundred and  seventy million dollars over the past  year mostly because of his popular  fashion line Yeezy the magazine  estimates his net worth at 1.3 billion  dollars  rounding out the top ten highest paid  celebs Roger Federer Cristiano Ronaldo  Lionel Messi Tyler Perry  Neymar Howard Stern LeBron James and  Dwyane Johnson Forbes was the first  publication to label Kylie a billionaire  back in 2019 and doubled down on the  claim she was a self-made billionaire in  2020 starting a company on my own and it  being so big from the beginning there's  not a lot of room for mistakes but in an  article published last month the mag  accused Kylie of lying about her  earnings for years and claimed that she  backed up the numbers with falsified tax  returns  Kylie hit up Twitter to straight-up deny  it  Kylie wrote in part quote I've never  asked for any title or tried to lie my  way there ever period that was my true  fans to know it's worth pointing out  that forbes is now estimating Kylie's  net worth to be nine hundred million  dollars it's not like that was  to her she figured that all out on  Monday a source told ET that now Kylie  just wants people to stop focusing on  how much money she has adding this whole  thing seems to be a clickbait attempt  for Forbes meanwhile Kylie's attorney  Michael Kampf released a statement about  the whole thing saying that the article  is filled with outright lies and  demanding that the mag issue a  retraction quote it is sad that of all  things forbes has devoted three  reporters to investigate the effect of  the coronavirus crisis on Kylie's net  worth we would not expect that from a  supermarket tabloid much less from  Forbes  [Music]
 

